Chapter: OpeningValueEffectUndeclared

 The manifest is derived from opening's declared type, so an
 effectful opening must declare its effects or it would ship an empty
 capability manifest and be denied every gated syscall at runtime.
 A value-binding opening (opening : T = body, no parameters) is
 checked the same as a function opening: block-read performs
 Device.Block, the declared Integer does not, so the def-boundary
 row-subset check rejects it. Declaring [Device.Block] Integer is the
 fix (see codex/test/apps/block-io-basic).

Section: Body
  opening : Integer = block-read 0
